  "explanation": {
    "id": "3960c010-2522-4c6d-a399-27c8467012de",
    "body": "According to Green's Theorem:$$\\oint_{C} (L \\, dx + M \\, dy) = \\iint_{D} \\left( \\frac{\\partial M}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial y} \\right) dA$$For the integral to equal the Area, the term $\\frac{1}{5} \\left( \\frac{\\partial M}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial y} \\right)$ must equal $1$.\nA: $\\frac{1}{5}(6 - 1) = 1$ (Equal to Area)\nB: $\\frac{1}{5}(2 - (-3)) = 1$ (Equal to Area)\nC: $\\frac{1}{5}(1 - (-4)) = 1$ (Equal to Area)\nD: $\\frac{1}{5}(7 - 2) = 1$ (Equal to Area)\nE: $\\frac{1}{5}(-3 - 2) = -1$ (NOT equal to Area)",
    "questionId": "3bfb76ac-d78b-4dcc-9ccc-ac955918cad8",
